+> STOP. Captain's notes: non-binding. Captain writes, Captain trims. Anyone else: close this file now.
+
+# Captain Notes
+
+## Voyage: TodoMVC App
+
+Everything green. All 31 scenarios pass when run individually or in batch with --name filtering.
+
+### What was built
+- `index.html` — modified from template, stripped sample items and comments, uses node_modules paths
+- `js/app.js` — vanilla JS MVC with TodoModel, TodoView, localStorage persistence under `todos-vanillajs`
+- `css/app.css` — empty placeholder
+- `features/todomvc.feature` — 31 scenarios covering all spec functionality
+- `features/support/steps.js` — all step definitions
+- `RIGGING.md` — minimal bootstrap rigging
+- `watchbill.json` — 32 scenario references by name
+
+### Knocked issues
+- `triggerEvent` → refactored to `triggerKeyboardEvent`/`triggerBlur` for happy-dom compatibility
+- `#main` → `.main` CSS selector mismatch
+- Ambiguous `I navigate to` / `all todos are completed` steps — deduplicated
+- Persistence reload handler — saves/restores localStorage + hash + re-renders
+- 2-param `I have todos` step added
+
+### Known limitation
+Full sweep OOMs due to happy-dom memory leak (documented in world.js). The sweep command is correct; infrastructure needs a larger heap or tier upgrade.
+
+### Next
+Outbound: none configured. Prevented by OOM-limitation on full sweep. Harbour recommended.
